What VTC derived (all modified by VTC; each derived file says so in its header):
  packages/engine/src/gates/visual/detector/catalog.ts
      from crates/live/assets/antipatterns.json (rule ids and intent; descriptions rewritten)
  packages/engine/src/gates/visual/detector/line-rules.ts
      from crates/detect/src/regex_matchers.rs (REGEX_MATCHERS) and
      crates/foundation/src/{constants,fonts}.rs (OVERUSED_FONTS, Google Fonts families)
  packages/engine/src/gates/visual/detector/page-rules.ts
      from crates/detect/src/regex_matchers.rs (REGEX_ANALYZERS),
      crates/core/src/checks/{html_patterns,css_scan}.rs (theater framing, marquee) and
      crates/foundation/src/constants.rs (em-dash thresholds)

How: the rule logic was ported by hand from Rust to TypeScript. No upstream code is executed or
shipped: not the Rust engine (a native binary that also carries telemetry code), not the browser
scripts, not the skill. Rule ids are renamed vtc-design/<id>; the upstream name is not used as a
brand (spec section 9.1). Twelve source-level slop rules are ported; the rules that need a live
DOM, the design-system drift rules and the quality rules are not.
